## Default Parameters
Give a parameter a default value with `=`:
```ts
function greet(name: string, greeting: string = "Hello"): string {
    return greeting + ", " + name;
}
greet("Steve");           // "Hello, Steve"
greet("Steve", "Hey");    // "Hey, Steve"
```

## Optional Parameters
Mark a parameter as optional with `?`. It becomes `undefined` if not passed:
```ts
function log(msg: string, prefix?: string): void {
    if (prefix) {
        console.log(prefix + ": " + msg);
    } else {
        console.log(msg);
    }
}
log("hello");            // hello
log("hello", "INFO");    // INFO: hello
```

Optional params must come after required params.


